1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:01,140
Look at this letter.

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:02,700
G.

3
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:07,480
G has two different sounds, just like c.

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:09,480
Listen to the first one.

5
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:10,960
Goat.

6
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:13,900
The g says /g/.

7
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:17,400
Now listen to the second one.

8
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:19,280
Gem.

9
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:22,120
The g says /j/.

10
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:26,620
The same letter, making two different sounds.

11
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:29,980
So how do we know which sound to say?

12
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:34,160
It is the same secret we used for c.

13
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:38,000
We look at the letter that comes after the g.

14
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:40,360
Here is the rule.

15
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:44,320
Do you remember our three special letters?

16
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:45,580
E.

17
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:46,760
I.

18
00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:47,780
Y.

19
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:56,620
When g sees e, i or y coming next, the g goes soft.

20
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:00,840
A soft g says /j/.

21
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:02,340
Listen.

22
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:03,440
/j/...

23
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:04,780
e...

24
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:06,360
m...

25
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,360
Gem!

26
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:13,880
The e comes right after the g, so this g is soft.

27
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:17,320
Here are more soft g words.

28
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:19,280
Giant.

29
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:21,160
Gym.

30
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:22,800
Magic.

31
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:27,660
You have met soft g before, at the end of words.

32
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:29,640
Cage.

33
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:31,660
Large.

34
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:33,360
Bridge.

35
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:37,610
Every one of those has a soft g too.

36
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:40,900
So what happens everywhere else?

37
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:45,420
Everywhere else, the g stays hard.

38
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:50,780
A hard g says /g/, deep in your throat.

39
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:52,580
Listen.

40
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:53,780
/g/...

41
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:55,220
u...

42
00:01:57,420 --> 00:01:58,560
m...

43
00:01:58,560 --> 00:01:58,760
Gum!

44
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:05,080
The u comes after the g, and u is not one of our three letters.

45
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:07,900
So this g stays hard.

46
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:11,490
Here are more hard g words.

47
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:12,860
Goat.

48
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:14,840
Glad.

49
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:16,620
Flag.

50
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,420
You're doing really well!

51
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:23,420
If you're enjoying this, please like this video and subscribe.

52
00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:26,700
Then we can keep making more videos for you.

53
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:30,610
But now I must tell you something important.

54
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:35,260
The g rule is not as tidy as the c rule.

55
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:39,740
With c, the rule works every single time.

56
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:44,380
With g, it works most of the time, but not always.

57
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:52,660
Some words have e or i after the g, and the g stays hard anyway.

58
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:54,740
Listen to these.

59
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:56,320
Get.

60
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:58,300
Give.

61
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:00,620
Girl.

62
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:02,260
Gift.

63
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:04,720
Begin.

64
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:06,760
Tiger.

65
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:11,040
Every one of them should be soft, but it is not!

66
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:15,760
These are little words you already say every day.

67
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:19,560
So learn them by sight, and they will never trick you.

68
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:23,120
And here is a trick that always helps.

69
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:29,560
If a word sounds strange with a soft g, try the hard g instead.

70
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:33,060
Your ears will tell you which one is right.

71
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:37,320
Now let's look at more soft g words.

72
00:03:38,660 --> 00:03:39,020
Gem.

73
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:40,820
Giant.

74
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:42,620
Gym.

75
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:44,420
Magic.

76
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:46,260
Cage.

77
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:48,240
Large.

78
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:54,000
Every one has e, i or y after the g.

79
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,830
Now let's look at the hard g words.

80
00:03:59,000 --> 00:03:59,200
Goat.

81
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:01,280
Gum.

82
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:03,200
Glad.

83
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:05,100
Flag.

84
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:07,240
Green.

85
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:09,460
Wagon.

86
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:16,040
Not one of them has e, i or y after the g.

87
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,760
Now it's your turn!

88
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:20,640
Here is the word.

89
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:22,160
Green.

90
00:04:23,140 --> 00:04:26,480
Is this g hard, or is it soft?

91
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:30,340
It is hard!

92
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:32,920
The r comes right after the g.

93
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:35,600
Let's remember it together.

94
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:44,140
Before e, i or y, the g is usually soft and says /j/.

95
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:49,800
Everywhere else, the g is hard and says /g/.

96
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:53,040
And don't forget our tricky friends.

97
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:54,380
Get.

98
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:56,160
Give.

99
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:58,120
Girl.

100
00:04:59,320 --> 00:04:59,580
Gift.

101
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:05,120
Every letter and every sound is inside the English Learning app.

102
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:06,800
Go and try it.

103
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,600
It's completely free!
